{"cases":[{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"0cfb9113fd4e259463e1b334be2815298728209edb417245debf7fa73d9d6f10"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002 claims that maintaining a persistent union-find over defeat-equivalence classes and recomputing only the strongly connected component of a changed edge preserves the exact fixed point under bounded edits, but this is false when cross-component reinstatement occurs. A suspended node in component A can be reinstated if an accepted node in component B defeats its attacker; after an edit in A that removes that defender, the attacker may resurface, causing the originally reinstated node to become suspended again. Because SRC_002 only recomputes the SCC local to the changed edge in A, it cannot propagate this change back to B, so the versioned label array retains a stale 'accepted' label for the node in B. This violates the determinism of the fixed point and the reinstatement-as-derived-property guarantee required by the problem, since the incremental result diverges from the recomputed-from-scratch grounded extension.","counterexample":[{"attack_edges":[{"from":"b","to":"a"},{"from":"a","to":"x"},{"from":"c","to":"a"}],"component_B_node":"x","components":{"A":["a"],"B":["b","x","c"]},"edit":"remove attack edge from node b (in component B) to node a (in component A)","explanation":"Initially c (accepted) attacks a, so a is suspended. Since a is suspended, it does not defeat x, and x has no other accepted attacker, so x is accepted. Now remove the edge b->a. A from-scratch recomputation still keeps a suspended because c->a still defeats a, so x remains accepted. But consider instead removing c->a: a becomes accepted (no undefeated attacker), which defeats x, so x becomes suspended. If c is in a different SCC/region than the changed edge c->a and SRC_002 does not recompute x's component, x's label stays 'accepted' — a divergence from the true fixed point.","initial_labels":{"a":"accepted","b":"accepted","c":"accepted","x":"suspended"},"node_a":"a (in component A)","node_b":"b (in component B)","node_x":"x (in component B, reinstated by b's state)"}],"target":"ad74cced7e4dc70720df6c83540529eb9904152accdd92214803d3bddc780ea7"}]}